taxis in Japan, as in other countries, run on meters.
the basic fare covers the first one point five to two kilometers. beyond that the fare goes up according to distance or time.
the basic fare varies depending on the size of the car.
between eleven at night and five in the morning, special high rates are applied.
taxis in Japan may be a little more expensive than in other countries.
but no tipping is necessary.
if you take a cab for a long distance, you don't have to pay for the return trip.
you don't have to pay extra for baggage, either.
